74:
75:    Input structure
76:    - The background is the dominant color.
77:    - One foreground color forms exactly one full row, column, main diagonal, or anti-diagonal reflection axis.
78:    - The remaining foreground colors include a unique least-populated color to copy.
79:
80:    Rule
81:    - Preserve the input grid.
82:    - Select every pixel of the unique smallest non-axis foreground color.
83:    - Reflect those pixels across the full straight axis and paint the reflected positions with the same color.
84:
85:    Key insight
86:    - The axis color marks the mirror line, while the color population chooses which set of objects is duplicated.
87:    """
