8:    Draw a foreground-color rectangular frame just inside the four marker pixels.
9:
10:    Input structure:
11:    - The grid has a dominant background color, one foreground drawing color, and one marker color.
12:    - The marker color appears exactly four times, with unique top, bottom, left, and right extrema.
13:    - The foreground drawing color is the only non-background, non-marker color.
14:
15:    Rule:
16:    - Use the min/max marker rows and columns as outside guides.
17:    - Paint the rectangle border from one row/column inside those marker extrema in the foreground color.
18:    - Preserve all existing pixels, including the markers and the original foreground object.
19:
20:    Key insight:
21:    - The four markers are control pixels for the frame sides; the existing foreground object supplies the color to draw with.
22:    """
