48:    - The other non-background color is a single 8-connected interior object whose area determines the flattened line length.
49:
50:    Rule:
51:    - If the guide pair is vertical, make a vertical object-colored line centered between those bars; otherwise use the analogous horizontal line.
52:    - The line length equals the number of interior object pixels and is centered on the split perpendicular guide bar.
53:    - Rebuild the guide color as the perpendicular center bar plus two full bars immediately beside the flattened object line.
54:
55:    Key insight:
56:    - The guide bars supply only the orientation and center; the interior object's pixel count supplies the length of the final one-cell-thick line.
